# What is NOT part of the pack.
#
# Distribution Spec §4 defines the pack as config/, defaultconfigs/, kubejs/,
# resourcepacks/, datapacks/, ftbquests/ and the manifest — the files that carry
# gameplay. Everything else in this repository is the operating layer: how we
# build the pack, not the pack itself.
#
# Without this file `packwiz refresh` indexes the whole repo, and a friend
# installing the pack downloads CLAUDE.md, the ADRs and the git hooks.

# ANCHOR EVERY DIRECTORY PATTERN WITH A LEADING SLASH.
#
# packwiz uses gitignore semantics, so a bare `scripts/` matches a directory of
# that name AT ANY DEPTH. It was silently excluding
#     config/hordes/data/hordes/horde_data/scripts/default.json
# which is the only script The Hordes has -- the one that swaps to the drowned
# spawn table in ocean biomes. Combined with data_version: -1 (which stops the
# mod regenerating its folder) the shipped pack would have carried a Hordes
# config with its script missing, and nothing would have said so.
#
# This is the second time this exact bug has happened here: `build/` in
# .gitignore once matched scripts/build/ and kept the build script out of git.
# Same shape, different file. Anchor them.

# --- the agent operating layer -----------------------------------------------
/.claude/
/.githooks/
/.github/
/scripts/
/Obsidian-minecraft-100day/

# --- documentation -----------------------------------------------------------
/docs/
*.md

# --- repo metadata -----------------------------------------------------------
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.packwizignore

# --- local build / runtime output --------------------------------------------
/build/
/dist/
/run/
/instance/
/logs/
/crash-reports/
/saves/
*.mrpack
*.zip
